    "rawResponseText": "This is a great question that touches on one of the most active areas of hotel development strategy. Below is a comprehensive overview of the hotel brands most commonly considered when an owner wants to affiliate an independent upper-upscale property through a conversion in North America, organized by parent company.\n\n---\n\n## Hotel Brands for Upper-Upscale Conversion in North America\n\nThe upper-upscale segment is the dominant tier for soft-brand and collection-brand conversions. \nThe upper-upscale segment has the largest number of soft-brand collection rooms, representing 63% of the total.\n \nSoft brand affiliation has been a particularly attractive route, with soft brand room growth running nearly 10 times the growth in room count for traditional brands over the past decade.\n\n\n---\n\n### 1. 🏨 Marriott International\n\nMarriott offers the most expansive suite of soft/collection brands for upper-upscale independents:\n\n- **Autograph Collection Hotels** – \nAutograph Collection, launched in 2010, sits at the mid-to-upper upscale level and gathers independent hotels with character that meet Marriott standards.\n\n- **Tribute Portfolio** – \nTribute Portfolio, launched by Starwood in 2015 and inherited by Marriott a year later, lowered the entry threshold to capture lifestyle independents that wouldn't qualify for Autograph.\n\n- **The Luxury Collection** – Though technically luxury, it is sometimes considered by upper-upscale full-service properties seeking to trade up. \nThe Luxury Collection covers grand hotels, resorts, and palaces at the luxury tier.\n\n\n\nWith its three-tier collection strategy that includes The Luxury Collection, Autograph Collection Hotels, and Tribute Portfolio brands, independent hoteliers have multiple options to leverage Marriott's powerful loyalty and distribution channels, whether through a new build or conversion hotel, depending on the location and physical product.\n\n\n---\n\n### 2. 🏨 Hilton Worldwide\n\nHilton is another top contender, with two primary upper-upscale/upscale collection brands:\n\n- **Curio Collection by Hilton** – \nCurio Collection is made up of hotels and resorts that offer authentic, curated experiences to discerning leisure travelers, specializing in local offerings paired with \"elevated amenities,\" combining the best of independent hotels with Hilton's rewards program.\n\n- **Tapestry Collection by Hilton** – \nTapestry Collection by Hilton is a gathering of independent hotels whose momentum is fueled by high conversion demand and a flexible model that allows independent hotels to join the Hilton system while preserving their local character.\n\n\n\nHilton launched its first soft brand, Curio Collection, in 2014, creating a collection of independent, upscale hotels.\n From the owner's perspective, \nCurio Collection is considered Hilton's answer to Autograph Collection, rapidly growing, and known for being slightly more pragmatic regarding property improvement plans (PIPs).\n\n\n---\n\n### 3. 🏨 Hyatt Hotels Corporation\n\n- **The Unbound Collection by Hyatt** – \nThe Unbound Collection by Hyatt is a portfolio of upper-upscale and luxury properties ranging from historic urban gems to revitalizing retreats and modern marvels, designed to attract owners and developers who want their properties to maintain a distinct character and brand name, but gain the power of Hyatt's robust distribution, operational, and marketing resources.\n\n- **Destination by Hyatt** – \nThe Destination by Hyatt brand is a portfolio of upper-upscale and luxury hotels, resorts, and residences that are individual yet connected by a commitment to draw on the spirit of each location.\n\n- **JdV by Hyatt** – \nHyatt also has JdV by Hyatt\n as a lifestyle-oriented soft brand option positioned in the upscale-to-upper-upscale range.\n\n---\n\n### 4. 🏨 IHG Hotels & Resorts\n\n- **Vignette Collection** – \nIHG has Vignette\n as its soft brand collection for independent, character-rich properties seeking the backing of IHG's loyalty and distribution network. \nIHG's broader portfolio includes upper-upscale names like InterContinental, Regent, Crowne Plaza, and Kimpton.\n\n\n---\n\n### 5. 🏨 Choice Hotels International\n\n- **Radisson Individuals** – \nChoice Hotels relaunched Radisson Individuals as an upper-upscale soft brand focused on full-service, boutique, and independent hotels that stand apart for their distinctive local character and superior guest service.\n \nChoice is extending the brand to owners for the first time, marking a step in the company's expansion in the upper-upscale tier at a time of rising consumer demand.\n\n- **Ascend Hotel Collection** – \nChoice's Ascend Hotel Collection actually predates Autograph by two years as the original soft brand concept.\n It serves upscale and upper-upscale independent properties seeking brand affiliation.\n\n---\n\n### 6. 🏨 Wyndham Hotels & Resorts\n\n- **Wyndham Grand** – Wyndham's flagship upper-upscale full-service brand, suitable for large full-service independent hotels.\n- **Registry Collection Hotels** – \nAn upper-upscale/luxury soft brand, exemplified by properties like The Mining Exchange in Colorado Springs, which is a boutique property housed in a historic gold rush–era building.\n\n- **Trademark Collection by Wyndham** – \nA soft-branded collection that preserves unique heritage, illustrated by properties like JH Adams Inn and a former cotton and flour mill converted into boutique stays.\n\n\n---\n\n### 7. 🏨 Accor\n\n- **MGallery** and **Emblems Collection** – \nAccor has MGallery and Emblems\n as its primary soft-brand options for independent upper-upscale boutique hotels, both emphasizing unique, story-driven properties.\n\n---\n\n## Key Takeaway\n\n\nSoft brand collections in the upper-upscale segment have delivered strong EBITDA margins, outperforming many full-service hotels. Lifestyle hotels of this type are typically affiliated with major brands like Marriott International, Hilton Worldwide Holdings, and IHG Hotels & Resorts.\n The most commonly considered brands for upper-upscale independent conversions in North America are:\n\n| Brand | Parent Company | Positioning |\n|---|---|---|\n| Autograph Collection | Marriott | Upper-Upscale Soft Brand |\n| Tribute Portfolio | Marriott | Upper-Upscale/Upscale Soft Brand |\n| Curio Collection | Hilton | Upper-Upscale Soft Brand |\n| Tapestry Collection | Hilton | Upscale/Upper-Upscale Soft Brand |\n| The Unbound Collection | Hyatt | Upper-Upscale/Luxury Soft Brand |\n| Destination by Hyatt | Hyatt | Upper-Upscale/Luxury Soft Brand |\n| Vignette Collection | IHG | Upper-Upscale Soft Brand |\n| Radisson Individuals | Choice Hotels | Upper-Upscale Soft Brand |\n| Ascend Hotel Collection | Choice Hotels | Upscale/Upper-Upscale Soft Brand |\n| Wyndham Grand | Wyndham | Upper-Upscale Full-Service |\n| Registry Collection | Wyndham | Upper-Upscale/Luxury Soft Brand |\n| MGallery / Emblems | Accor | Upper-Upscale Soft Brand |\n\nThe brand decision ultimately hinges on factors such as the loyalty program's size and reach, property improvement plan (PIP) requirements, fee structures, and the owner's strategic distribution priorities.",
